====================================================================================================
|E e^{is(I-p)}|^2 - (1-2r(1-cos s)) = 0
max over x in [0,1] of sqrt(1-x) - exp(-x/2) = 0.0 (<=0: |factor| <= exp(-r(1-cos s)))
   note 2r(1-cos s) <= 4r <= 1 so x stays in [0,1].
2000 random (population,t,u): violations of |H0|<=D: 0; max |H0|/D = 0.999996
max relative error in  r sum s_i^2 = t'Sigma_n t + u^2 : 8.58e-16
min eigenvalue of Gram matrix [D(tau_a-tau_b)] on 60 random points of R^{N+1}: 0.12780217829827756 (>= 0 up to rounding: D is positive definite, as it must be for a c.f.)
exp(r(cos x -1)) = E exp(i x (P1-P2)), P1,P2 iid Poisson(r/2): 0
tent test (lattice population -1/2, n=30,b=10): centered integral 1.17412; max over 300 random shifts 1.09063;
   at the resonance (t,u)=(2 pi h/3)(1,1): D = 1.000000, |H_0| = 1.000000, shifted tent integral 1.17412
   -> the bound int_{cube} D <= C is attained at resonances: |Psi_0| is NOT small in L^1(Q_j); only boundedness is available, as the proof uses.

