ITEM 3. small frequencies: cumulants, uniform remainder, u-integration
====================================================================================================
cumulant 2: -p*(p - 1)   minus r: 0
cumulant 3: p*(p - 1)*(2*p - 1)   minus r d: 0
cumulant 4: -p*(p - 1)*(6*p**2 - 6*p + 1)   minus r d4: 0
cumulant 5: p*(p - 1)*(2*p - 1)*(12*p**2 - 12*p + 1)  -> divisible by p(1-p): -(2*p - 1)*(12*p**2 - 12*p + 1)
sup_p sup_{rho/4<|s|<=0.25} |remainder| / (r |s|^5) = 0.00833   (bounded uniformly in p; limit value |kappa_5|/(120 r) <= 1/120=0.00833)
sup_p sup_{rho/4<|s|<=0.5} |remainder| / (r |s|^5) = 0.00833   (bounded uniformly in p; limit value |kappa_5|/(120 r) <= 1/120=0.00833)
sup_p sup_{rho/4<|s|<=1.0} |remainder| / (r |s|^5) = 0.00833   (bounded uniformly in p; limit value |kappa_5|/(120 r) <= 1/120=0.00833)
limit of f/(p(1-p)) at p=0: -z + exp(z) - 1    at p=1: z - 1 + exp(-z)   (both entire in z: no singularity is created)
E_u A_3 = I*(-3*m_1 - m_3)   -> with m_1=0: -I*m_3  = n^{-1} sum (i a_l)^3
E_u A_4 (m_1=0) = 6*m_2 + m_4 + 3
E_u A_3^2 (m_1=0) = -9*m_2**2 - 18*m_2 - m_3**2 - 15
order eps^2 coefficient after u-integration  R(t) = -d**2*m_2**2/8 - d**2*m_2/4 - d**2*m_3**2/72 - 5*d**2/24 + d_4*m_2/4 + d_4*m_4/24 + d_4/8
R(0) = -5*d**2/24 + d_4/8   with d^2=1-4r, d4=1-6r: r/12 - 1/12  (= -(1-r)/12, matches the local-limit expansion above)
Q_n(t) = R(t)-R(0) = -d**2*m_2**2/8 - d**2*m_2/4 - d**2*m_3**2/72 + d_4*m_2/4 + d_4*m_4/24
Q_n with d4-d^2 = -2r: quadratic part = -r/2 * m_2   => covariance (1 + eps^2 r) Sigma_n = (1+1/n) Sigma_n, consistent with exact n/(n-1) Sigma_n to O(n^-2)

